  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a binary string SSS of length NNN.\n\nDefine:\n\n\ncnt00cnt_{00}cnt00​ = the number of substrings `00` in SSS.\ncnt11cnt_{11}cnt11​ = the number of substrings `11` in SSS.\nIn one **flip**, you may choose any index iii and toggle SiS_iSi​ (`0` becomes `1`, `1` becomes `0`).\n\nYour task is to determine the **minimum number of flips** required to make cnt11≥cnt00cnt_{11} \\ge cnt_{00}cnt11​≥cnt00​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of **two lines**:\n\nThe first line contains an integer NNN — the length of the binary string.\nThe second line contains the binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of flips required to make cnt11≥cnt00cnt_{11} \\ge cnt_{00}cnt11​≥cnt00​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "7\n2\n00\n2\n01\n2\n10\n2\n11\n3\n001\n3\n101\n3\n000",
        "output": "1\n0\n0\n0\n1\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nFor the first test case, we can flip the first zero achieving 10.\n\nNow, cnt11=0cnt_{11} = 0cnt11​=0 is greater than or equal to cnt00=0cnt_{00} = 0cnt00​=0.\n\n\n\nFor the second test case, we make no flips achieving 01.\n\nNow, cnt11=0cnt_{11} = 0cnt11​=0 is greater than or equal to cnt00=0cnt_{00} = 0cnt00​=0.\n\n\n\nFor the fifth test case, we flip the second zero achieving 011.\n\nNow, cnt11=1cnt_{11} = 1cnt11​=1 is greater than or equal to cnt00=0cnt_{00} = 0cnt00​=0."
      }
    ]
  },
